Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Erosion Control Works Act and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended 2007.3.22, 2009.3.25>

Article 2 (Public Notice of Designation and Cancellation of Erosion Control Areas) Where the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or the Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as “Mayor/Do Governor”), or the head of a regional forest service designates or changes an erosion control area or cancels its designation under Article 4 or 20 of the Erosion Control Works Act (hereinafter referred to as the “Act”), he or she shall publicly notify the following: <Amended 2002.3.2, 2007.3.22, 2008.1.31, 2011.12.30, 2017.11.14>
1. The parcel numbers, land categories, and areas of the land designated, changed, or released from designation;
2. The grounds for designation, change, or cancellation;
3. The types of works subject to designation, change, or cancellation;
4. The date of designation, change, or cancellation;
5. A drawing clearly indicating the erosion control area designated, changed, or released from designation on a topographic map showing cadastral information, a cadastral map, etc.

Article 2-2 (Scale Exempt from Designation as an Erosion Control Area) The scale that need not be designated as an erosion control area under Article 4 (3) of the Act means mountain erosion control works under Article 3, subparagraph 1 of the Act with an area of not more than 1,000 square meters at each site.
[This Article newly inserted 2008.1.31]

Article 3 (Implementers of National Erosion Control Works) Erosion control works implemented as national projects under Article 5 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as “national erosion control works”) shall be implemented by the Mayor/Do Governor in erosion control areas other than national forests under the jurisdiction of the Korea Forest Service, and by the head of the regional forest service in erosion control areas that are national forests under the jurisdiction of the Korea Forest Service. <Amended 2006.1.26, 2008.1.31, 2011.12.30>
[Wholly amended 2002.3.2]

Article 4 (Implementation of Erosion Control Works by Persons Other than the State)
(1) An erosion control works plan to be submitted where a person other than the State implements erosion control works under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall contain the following matters: <Amended 2008.1.31>
1. The purpose of implementing the erosion control works;
2. The type of erosion control works;
3. The volume of works (area) for each parcel number.
(2) A person intending to implement erosion control works under paragraph (1) shall submit the following documents: <Amended 2008.1.31, 2009.3.25, 2009.12.14, 2015.6.1, 2015.11.11, 2025.2.7>
1. One copy of an actual survey drawing of the erosion control works site, at a scale from 1:6,000 to 1:1,200, surveyed by any of the following:
(a) The Korea Land and Geospatial Informatix Corporation under the Korea Land and Geospatial Informatix Corporation Act;
(b) A surveying business entity under Article 44 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
(c) Deleted. <2009.12.14>
2. One copy of a document proving ownership of the land or the right to use and profit from it (only where this cannot be verified through a certificate of registered matters for the land; a document proving the right to use and profit shall state the scope and duration of that right in detail).
(3) Upon receiving an erosion control works plan under paragraph (1), the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service shall verify the certificate of registered matters for the land (only where the applicant is the landowner) through shared use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act. <Newly inserted 2008.1.31; amended 2009.3.25, 2010.5.4, 2011.12.30, 2015.11.11>
[Wholly amended 1999.3.3]

Article 4-2 (Feasibility Assessment of Erosion Control Works) The standards, methods, projects subject to assessment, etc. for feasibility assessments under Article 7-3 of the Act shall be as set out in attached Table 1.
[This Article newly inserted 2008.1.31]

Article 5 (Investigations by Public Officials)
(1) Where a public official intends to enter another person's land to conduct surveys or investigations or alter or remove obstacles under Article 9 (1) of the Act, the official shall notify the owner and possessor in advance. <Amended 2002.3.2>
(2) Where an implementer of national erosion control works intends to perform any act under the subparagraphs of Article 9 (3) of the Act, the implementer shall notify the owners and possessors of the relevant land, standing trees, etc. of the purpose, details, duration, etc. of the act no later than seven days before performing it. <Amended 2014.2.18>
(3) In cases under paragraphs (1) and (2), where notice cannot be given because the address or residence of an owner or possessor is unknown or for another reason, the matters to be notified shall be notified to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of the Si/Gun/Gu (a head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; the same applies hereinafter) having jurisdiction over the location of the land or object. <Amended 2008.1.31, 2011.12.30, 2014.2.18, 2017.11.14>
(4) The Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of the Si/Gun/Gu receiving notice under paragraph (3) shall publicly announce it. <Amended 2011.12.30, 2017.11.14>
[Title amended 2014.2.18]

Article 6 (Restoration) Where loss occurs due to an act under Article 9 (1) or (3) of the Act, the relevant implementer of erosion control works shall carry out necessary work, including leveling topsoil to restore land whose form and quality have been altered, supplementary planting of standing trees or bamboo, or sowing turf or grass. <Amended 2002.3.2>
[Title amended 2002.3.2]

Article 7 (Application for and Determination of Compensation for Loss)
(1) A person seeking compensation for loss under Article 10 (1) of the Act shall submit an application stating the following to the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service who performed the act causing the loss, within six months after the date on which that act ended: <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26, 2014.2.18>
1. The claimant's name and address and the date of claim;
2. The addresses and names of the landowner and persons concerned;
3. The location, parcel number, land category, and area of the land affected by the loss;
4. The type of loss and its area or quantity;
5. The period during which the loss occurred;
6. The amount of compensation sought and its breakdown;
7. Documents proving that the loss was suffered.
(2) Within one month after receiving an application under paragraph (1), the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service shall determine the amount of compensation through consultation with the person who suffered the loss and notify the applicant of the payment date, payment method, etc. <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>

Article 8 (Application for Adjudication) Where consultation on compensation under Article 7 (2) fails, or there is an objection to the amount determined as compensation for loss, the person who suffered the loss and the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service shall, under Article 12 of the Act, apply for adjudication to the land expropriation committee having jurisdiction over the land, attaching a statement of reasons, within one year after the date on which the act causing the loss ended. <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>

Article 9 (Deposit of Compensation for Loss) A Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall deposit compensation for loss in any of the following cases: <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>
1. Where the person entitled to compensation refuses or evades receipt of it;
2. Where compensation cannot be paid because the address or residence of the person entitled to it is unknown or for another reason.

Article 10 (Hearing Opinions of Appraisers)
(1) Where deemed necessary in determining the amount of compensation under Article 7 (2), a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service may hear the opinions of appraisers, witnesses, or interested parties. <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>
(2) Travel expenses may be paid to appraisers and witnesses appearing under paragraph (1), as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended 1996.8.8, 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>

Article 11 (Restrictions on Activities in Erosion Control Areas) A person intending to fell standing trees or bamboo or perform other acts in an erosion control area under the main clause of Article 14 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for permission, attaching documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, the head of the Si/Gun/Gu, or the head of the regional forest service. The same applies when intending to extend the permission period.
[Wholly amended 2023.11.16]

Article 12 (Management of Erosion Control Facilities) Matters necessary for the management, inspection, safety diagnosis, and safety measures for erosion control facilities under Article 15 (3) of the Act shall be as set out in attached Table 2.
[Wholly amended 2008.1.31]

Article 13 (Distribution of Benefits)
(1) The rates at which a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall distribute benefits arising from erosion control facilities installed through national erosion control works to the owner and possessor of the erosion control area and the manager of the facilities under Article 17 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended 2007.3.22>
1. Owner and possessor of the erosion control area: 10 percent;
2. Manager of the erosion control facilities: 90 percent.
(2) A Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall notify the persons entitled to distribution in advance of the rate or quantity of benefits to be distributed under paragraph (1). The same applies when intending to change the rate or quantity to be distributed. <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>
(3) Where notice under paragraph (2) cannot be given because the address or residence of a person entitled to distribution is unknown or for another reason, a public announcement shall be made.
(4) The timing and procedures for distributing benefits calculated at the rates under paragraph (1), and other necessary matters, shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended 1996.8.8, 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>

Article 14 (Deposit of Distributed Benefits) In any of the following cases, a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall sell the benefits to be distributed under Article 13 and deposit the proceeds: <Amended 1995.12.29, 2002.3.2, 2006.1.26>
1. Where a person entitled to distribution refuses or evades receipt;
2. Where distribution is impossible because the address or residence of the person entitled to it is unknown or for another reason.

Article 15 Deleted. <2007.3.22>

Article 16 Deleted. <2011.12.30>

Article 17 (Cancellation of Designation of Erosion Control Areas)
(1) A person intending to obtain cancellation of the designation of an erosion control area on any ground under Article 20 (1) 1 through 4 of the Act shall submit an application for cancellation to the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service, attaching documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended 1996.8.8, 2008.2.29, 2011.12.30, 2013.3.23, 2014.2.18>
(2) Upon receiving an application under paragraph (1), a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall examine its validity and cancel the designation if the application is deemed appropriate; where an erosion control area falls under Article 20 (1) 5 or 6 of the Act, he or she shall cancel the designation ex officio after an on-site investigation. In such cases, for an erosion control area falling under Article 20 (1) 5 of the Act and paragraph (4) 1 of this Article, the opinion of an inspection institution under subparagraph 2 (c) of attached Table 2 shall be heard in addition to an on-site investigation. <Amended 2011.12.30, 2025.3.11>
(3) “Project prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 20 (1) 4 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended 2014.2.18>
1. Public works such as railways, ports, airports, roads, and land reclamation;
2. Projects implemented directly by the State or a local government or implemented through entrustment;
3. Soil dressing projects to improve the fertility of farmland;
4. Soil and stone collection projects deemed particularly necessary for policy purposes by the head of a local government.
(4) “Where the purpose of designation of the erosion control area prescribed by Presidential Decree has been achieved” in Article 20 (1) 5 of the Act means where an erosion control area falling under either of the following no longer requires continued management as an erosion control area, because the ground has been stabilized by erosion control facilities or for similar reasons: <Amended 2014.2.18, 2025.3.11, 2026.1.30>
1. An erosion control area for which one year has elapsed since implementation of the erosion control works;
2. An erosion control area whose designation as a landslide-prone area has been cancelled under Article 22 (8) of the Forest Disaster Prevention Act.
(5) “Where the purpose of designation of the erosion control area prescribed by Presidential Decree has ceased to exist” in Article 20 (1) 6 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended 1999.3.3, 2014.2.18>
1. Where land surrounding the erosion control area has been developed for a purpose other than forestry and retention as an erosion control area is deemed unnecessary;
2. Where erosion control facilities have disappeared or been submerged due to changes in land form caused by moving sand dunes or other natural conditions, and erosion control works need not be implemented again;
3. Where water flow in a stream or river at a torrent erosion control works site has changed due to natural phenomena or development for another purpose, and retention as an erosion control area is deemed unnecessary.

Article 18 (Transfer of Erosion Control Facilities without Charge) When intending to transfer erosion control facilities to the landowner without charge under Article 20 (3) of the Act, a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall notify the landowner of that fact.
[Wholly amended 2008.1.31]

Article 19 (Reimbursement of Expenses)
(1) Expenses to be reimbursed by a person intending to obtain cancellation of the designation of an erosion control area under Article 21 of the Act shall be as follows:
1. The amount spent on implementing the erosion control works;
2. Cash expenditures recognized by the head of the local government for repairing erosion control facilities, topdressing, pest and disease control, tending, forest fire prevention, and other equivalent expenses.
(2) Reimbursement under paragraph (1) shall accrue to the manager of the erosion control facilities. <Amended 2008.1.31>
(3) Cases exempt from reimbursement of expenses upon cancellation of the designation of an erosion control area under the proviso to Article 21 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended 1999.3.3, 2000.3.13, 2000.7.27, 2002.3.2, 2002.12.31, 2003.6.30, 2003.11.29, 2003.12.30, 2004.6.29, 2005.3.18, 2006.8.4, 2007.3.22, 2007.3.27, 2009.12.15, 2013.4.22, 2015.7.20, 2015.11.11, 2017.3.29, 2018.2.9, 2020.9.10, 2021.3.30, 2022.6.14>
1. Improvement of living environments in agricultural and fishing villages and development of rural tourism and recreational areas under the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act;
2. Installation by nonprofit corporations of medical institutions in agricultural and fishing village areas under the Medical Service Act and social welfare facilities under the Social Welfare Services Act;
3. Construction of dams under the Act on Construction and Management of Dams and Assistance to Their Surrounding Areas;
4. Installation or improvement of power supply facilities under the Electric Power Source Development Promotion Act;
5. Redevelopment projects and residential environment improvement projects under the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments, and construction of housing no larger than the national housing size with approval of a project implementation plan under Article 50 of that Act (limited to reconstruction projects);
6. Construction of housing no larger than the national housing size with approval of a project plan under the Housing Act;
7. Incheon International Airport development projects implemented under the Airport Facilities Act;
8. Construction of railway facilities under the Korea National Railway Act;
9. Installation of youth training facilities under Article 10, subparagraph 1 of the Youth Activity Promotion Act;
10. Development of industrial complexes designated under the Industrial Sites and Development Act;
11. Installation of performance halls under the Public Performance Act;
12. Installation of private museums or private art museums whose establishment plans have been approved under the Museum and Art Museum Support Act;
12-2. Installation of private science museums whose establishment plans have been approved under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Promotion of Science Museums;
13. Installation of private libraries under the Libraries Act;
14. Facilities intended to promote culture and arts under the Culture and Arts Promotion Act;
15. Facilities for educational or research purposes of specific research institutions under the Specific Research Institutes Support Act and research institutions established under special Acts;
16. Facilities of schools at all levels under the Elementary and Secondary Education Act and the Higher Education Act;
17. Installation of telecommunications facilities under the Telecommunications Business Act;
18. Installation of electric installations under the Electric Utility Act and the Electrical Safety Management Act;
19. Establishment of natural recreation forests under the Forestry Culture and Recreation Act and arboretums and gardens under the Act on the Creation and Furtherance of Arboretums and Gardens;
20. Public convenience facilities under development plans for tourist destinations, etc. under Article 46 (1) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Tourism Promotion Act;
20-2. Construction of national expressways under the Road Act;
20-3. Construction of urban railways under the Urban Railroad Act;
20-4. Construction of water supply facilities under the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act;
21. Projects to develop sites for public facilities donated to the State or a local government under relevant statutes or conditions of authorization, permission, etc. (including cases where they revert to the State or a local government without charge under statutes);
22. Rural housing and its ancillary facilities constructed by the State or a local government;
23. Sites for reservoirs, small reservoirs, waterways, farmland improvement, and similar facilities, and land to be submerged thereby;
24. Where farmers, foresters, fishers, or producers' organizations for agricultural, forestry, or fishery products intend to use the area for any of the following purposes:
(a) Construction of farming or fishing household housing and installation of its ancillary facilities;
(b) Development of farmland or grassland;
(c) Installation of farm roads;
(d) Installation of facilities related to the production, processing, etc. of forest products;
(e) Installation of wild bird and animal breeding facilities, livestock facilities, silkworm rearing facilities, mushroom cultivation facilities, fixed agricultural greenhouses, fish farms, aquaculture farms, agricultural machinery repair facilities, agricultural machinery warehouses, warehouses, collection centers or processing facilities for agricultural, forestry, livestock, and fishery products, or facilities manufacturing organic fertilizer using livestock manure.

Article 20 (Keeping of Official Registers)
(1) A Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a regional forest service shall keep erosion control works registers and other records prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended 1995.12.29, 1996.8.8, 2006.1.26, 2007.12.31, 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
(2) Erosion control works registers and other records under paragraph (1) shall be prepared and managed in a manner enabling electronic processing, unless there is a special reason that makes electronic processing impossible. <Newly inserted 2007.12.31>

Article 21 (Inspection of Registers) Forest owners and other interested parties may request the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of the regional forest service to allow inspection of erosion control works registers and other records under Article 20 or issue certified copies thereof. <Amended 2006.1.26>
[Wholly amended 1999.3.3]

Article 21-2 Deleted. <2026.1.30>

Article 22 (Delegation of Authority)
(1) Deleted. <2011.12.30>
(2) Deleted. <2008.1.31>
(3) The head of a regional forest service shall delegate the following powers to the heads of national forest management offices of that regional forest service under Article 25 (2) of the Act: <Amended 2009.3.25, 2014.2.18>
1. Implementation of erosion control works under Article 5 (2) of the Act (excluding design);
2. Construction of erosion control works under Article 7-2 (1) of the Act;
3. Entry onto land, alteration and removal of obstacles, temporary use and alteration of the form and quality of land, and collection of standing trees, etc. under Article 9 (1) and (3) of the Act (excluding entry, etc. for design purposes);
4. Compensation for loss under Article 10 (1) of the Act;
5. Consultation under Article 11 of the Act;
6. Permission under Article 14 of the Act to fell standing trees or bamboo, collect soil, stones, tree roots, or grass roots, graze livestock, otherwise damage or alter erosion control facilities, or change the form and quality of land in erosion control areas;
7. Distribution of benefits arising from erosion control facilities under Article 17 of the Act;
8. Deleted. <2011.12.30>
9. Entrustment of the implementation of erosion control works under Article 26 of the Act (excluding design).
[Wholly amended 2002.3.2]

Article 23 (Entrusted Implementation of Erosion Control Works) Erosion control works that may be entrusted to a forestry cooperative or its federation under Article 26 of the Act shall comprise the design and construction of mountain, coastal, and torrent erosion control works. <Amended 2000.5.1>

Article 24 (Review of Regulations) The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service shall review the appropriateness of the following matters every three years from the relevant base date below (meaning before the same date as the base date in every third year) and take measures for improvement, etc.:
1. The scope of projects for which the designation of erosion control areas may be cancelled for collecting soil and stones under Article 17 (3): January 1, 2016;
2. The scope of exemption from reimbursement of expenses upon cancellation of the designation of erosion control areas under Article 19 (3): January 1, 2016.
[Wholly amended 2016.12.30]

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 14409, 1994.11.3>
(1) (Enforcement Date) This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
